;;; core.sheaf -- sheaf theory on finite sites as one library.
;;;
;;; Usage: (require core.sheaf)
;;;
;;; Loads the whole facility (each part can also be required alone):
;;;   core.integer_linalg     Smith normal form, integer kernels, lattices,
;;;                           cochain cohomology with torsion and generators
;;;   core.sheaf.site         finite categories, sieves, Grothendieck
;;;                           topologies, sites, finite (Alexandrov) spaces
;;;   core.sheaf.glue         gluing results, covers of data by pieces,
;;;                           gluing with named obstructions
;;;   core.sheaf.presheaf     presheaves of sets: matching families, the
;;;                           sheaf condition, the plus construction
;;;   core.sheaf.module       presheaves of free Z-modules and Q-vector
;;;                           spaces: sheaf condition, gluing, plus construction
;;;   core.sheaf.cohomology   Cech cohomology, sheaves on finite spaces by
;;;                           stalks, derived limits, cocycle generators
;;;
;;; Reference: docs/reference/stdlib/sheaf.md; design: ADR-0033
;;; (docs/design/adr/0033-core-sheaf-finite-sites.md).
;;; Sources: SGA 4 (Expose I-V); R. Godement, "Topologie algebrique et
;;; theorie des faisceaux" (1958); S. Mac Lane, I. Moerdijk, "Sheaves in
;;; Geometry and Logic" (1992); G. E. Bredon, "Sheaf Theory" (1997);
;;; B. Iversen, "Cohomology of Sheaves" (1986).

(require core.integer_linalg)
(require core.sheaf.site)
(require core.sheaf.glue)
(require core.sheaf.presheaf)
(require core.sheaf.module)
(require core.sheaf.cohomology)
